# Miscellaneous
# Bare ".env" only matches the repository root, so backend/.env was being copied
# into the production image. It carries local development values - including a
# Django secret key, a database password, a Paystack secret and a REDIS_URL -
# and python-dotenv loads it at startup, overriding what the platform provides.
# That is how production ended up trying to reach a Redis that does not exist,
# with local secrets baked into a registry image.
.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
*.log
*.pot
.cache/
